                  }
          %p
            One characteristic property is that the two outer sequences are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequences"} exact sequences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            on trivial bundles whose curvature vanishes in that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{d}A = 0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connections"} flat connections
            have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion
            Chern-clases.
          %p
            So a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            theory would be one whose
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+classes"} cohomology classes
            have the interpretation of (stable)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} principal ∞-bundles
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} connection
            such as in the middle of this diagram.
          %p
            The characterization/construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+products"} homotopy fiber products
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spectra"} mapping spectra
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            data) due to (
            %a{:href => "#HopkinsSinger02"}> Hopkins-Singer 02
            ) provides an incarnation of this kind of diagram genuinely in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequences"} homotopy fiber sequences
            and the two squares are homotopy cartesian (are
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullbacks"} homotopy pullbacks
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushouts"} homotopy pushouts
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13"}> Bunke-Nikolaus-Völkl 13
            ) it was observed (see
            %a{:href => "#Schreiber13"} Schreiber 13, section 4.1.2
            for the generality in which we present this here) that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+type"} stable homotopy type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            canonically sits inside a diagram of this form, being formed from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fracture+squares"} fracture squares
            of the units and counits of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_E
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ch
                      %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ch_E
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Π
                            %mi dR
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi d
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi dR
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↗
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi θ
                                  %mover
                                    %mi E
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Π
                            %mi dR
                          %mo ♭
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Π
                          %msub
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi dR
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↗
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ch
                                  %mi E
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ♭
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Π
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp;  \Pi_{dR} {\hat E} &amp;&amp; \stackrel{\mathbf{d}}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; \flat_{dR}{\hat E}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \nearrow &amp; &amp; \searrow &amp; &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\theta_{\hat E}}} &amp;&amp; \searrow
                  \\\
                  \\Pi_{dR} \flat  {\hat E}  &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; {\hat E} &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \Pi \flat_{dR}  \hat E
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;  &amp; \nearrow &amp; &amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{ch_E}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \flat {\hat E} &amp;&amp; \longrightarrow &amp;&amp; \Pi \hat E
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheDifferentialDiagram"}
            below.
          %p
            For the special case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %mi T
                  %mi Smooth
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} = T Smooth\infty Grpd
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} tangent (∞,1)-topos
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth ∞-groupoids
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#HopkinsSinger02"} Hopkins-Singer 02
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+types"} stable homotopy types
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            (see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Schreiber13"} Schreiber 13
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13"} BunkeNikolausVölkl 13
          %p
            Therefore it makes sense to define generally that a
            %em differential cohomology diagram
            is the above combined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fracture+squares"} fracture squares
            with its outer
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequences"} homotopy fiber sequences
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
            in any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
          %h2#definitionconstruction Definition/Construction
          %h3#differential_coefficients_and_maurercartan_forms Differential coefficients and Maurer-Cartan forms
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\mathbf{H}
            for its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} tangent cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            and write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi T
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_\ast \mathbf{H} \hookrightarrow T \mathbf{H}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+objects"} spectrum objects
            inside it.
          %p As usual, we use the following notation.
          #DifferentialCoefficients.num_defn
            %h6#definition_notation Definition (Notation)
            %p Write
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ♭
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
            %p
              restricted to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Stab
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi T
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab(\mathbf{H}) \hookrightarrow  T \mathbf{H}
            %p
              Given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spectra"} Spectra
              we say that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Stab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E \in Stab(\mathbf{H})
              with an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Pi(\hat E) \simeq E
            %p
              is a
              %em cohesive refinement
              or
              %em differential refinement
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %p Write
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ♭
                          %mi dR
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR}
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
                  of the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ♭
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+a+comonad"} counit
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mi dR
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_{dR}
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofiber"} homotopy cofiber
                  of the looping of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Π
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi θ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi id
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msub
                          %mo ♭
                          %mi dR
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta \;\colon\; id \longrightarrow \flat_{dR}
                  for the canonical morphism (itself the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
                  of
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi dR
                          %mo →
                          %mo ♭
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR} \to \flat
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
            %p
              Notice that on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+types"} stable homotopy types
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi cofib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\flat_{dR}A \simeq cofib(\flat A \to A) =  A/(\flat A)
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Warning: Elsewhere we often write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR} \Sigma
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR}
              above and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mi dR
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_{dR}\Omega
              for what is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mi dR
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_{dR}
              here. That other convention has its advanages in the context of unstable cohesion. Here with stable cohesion the present convention is more natural.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              As discussed at
              %em
                %a{:href => "cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos+--+structures#deRhamCohomology"} structures in a cohesive ∞-topos – de Rham cohomology
              there (and as is discussed below at
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#DeRhamCoefficients"} de Rham coefficients
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                      %mo *
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathbf{T}_\ast H
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type"} cohesive homotopy type
              then we may think of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mi dR
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_{dR} A
              and of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR}  A
              as being the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mo ♭
                        %mi dR
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(\flat_{dR} \Sigma A)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mi dR
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi d
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ♭
                              %mi dR
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Pi_{dR}A &amp;&amp; \stackrel{\mathbf{d}}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; \flat_{dR}A
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \nearrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; A
                    }
            %p
              interpreting as the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+differential"} de Rham differential
            %p
              Beware that this is a very general conceptualization of de Rham coefficients. In standard examples
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR}
              does come from traditional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
              data (see at
              %em
                %a{:href => "#DeligneCoefficients"} Deligne coefficients
              and at
              %em
                %a{:href => "#HopkinsSingerCoefficients"} Hopkins-Singer coefficients
              below), but generally it may have quite different looking models. But in any case
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR} \Sigma A
              always has the interpretation of the home of the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature+forms"} curvature forms
              of cohomology with coefficients in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR}
              as producing generalized form data useful.
          %h3#ChernCharacterAndFractureSquares Chern character and the differential fracture squares
          #GeneralChernCharacter.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
              = succeed "," do
