          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intermediate+Jacobian"} intermediate Jacobian
          %h2#References References
          %p
            The differential cohomology hexagon was maybe first highlighted in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
          %ul
            %li#SimonsSullivan07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Simons"}> James Simons
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Sullivan"} Dennis Sullivan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Axiomatic Characterization of Ordinary Differential Cohomology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0701077"} arXiv:math/0701077
          %p
            and in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
            in
          %ul
            %li#SimonsSullivan08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Simons"}> James Simons
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Sullivan"} Dennis Sullivan
              %em Structured vector bundles define differential K-theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0810.4935"}> arXiv:0810.4935
              )
          %p discussed also in
          %ul
            %li#FreedLott10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Lott"} John Lott
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An index theorem in differential K-theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~lott/gt-2010-14-021p.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Jiahao Hu,
                %em Characterization of differential K-theory by hexagon diagram
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.04925"}> arXiv:2209.04925
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            An artistic impression of the differential cohomology hexagon as a dance choreography inspired by a talk by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Simons"} James Simons
            is at
          %ul
            %li
              Kyla Barkin, Aaron Selissen,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Differential Cohomology
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://vimeo.com/32903887"} full video (37 min)
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.dancemedia.com/v/7044"} sequence of “The March Back” (4 min)
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.businessinsider.com/jim-simons-mathematical-genius-inspired-a-ballet-2011-1"} press release
          %p
            That the differential cohomology hexagon exists not just at the level of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequences"} exact sequences
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+classes"} cohomology classes
            but already at the level of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequences"} homotopy fiber sequences
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            spaces was observed for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            and for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
            in
          %ul
            %li
              Man-Ho Ho,
              %em Refined hexagons for differential cohomology
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.0582"}> arXiv:1310.0582
              )
          %p
            That generally the
            = succeed "-construction" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+product"} homotopy fiber product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            theories due to
          %ul
            %li#HopkinsSinger02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"} Mike Hopkins
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isadore+Singer"} Isadore Singer
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quadratic+Functions+in+Geometry%2C+Topology%2Cand+M-Theory"} Quadratic Functions in Geometry, Topology,and M-Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0211216"}> arXiv:math/0211216
              )
          %p constitutes the right one of the two squares in the homotopy-theoretic version of the diagram is discussed explicitly for instance in prop 4.57 of
          %ul
            %li#Bunke12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              %em Differential cohomology
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1208.3961"}> arXiv:1208.3961
              )
          %p
            That every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+type"} stable homotopy type
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            naturally sits in a differential cohomology diagram was observed (focusing on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
          %ul
            %li#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"} Thomas Nikolaus
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+V%C3%B6lkl"} Michael Völkl
              = succeed "," do
                %em Differential cohomology theories as sheaves of spectra
              %strong 11
              (2016) 1–66
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.3188"} arXiv:1311.3188
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s40062-014-0092-5"} doi:10.1007/s40062-014-0092-5
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p following
          %ul
            %li#Schreiber13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.7930"}> arXiv:1310.7930
              )
          %p where in section 4.1.2 a fully general abstract account is given. This in turn follows
          %ul
            %li#Schreiber09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Background+fields+in+twisted+differential+nonabelian+cohomology"} Background fields in twisted differential nonabelian cohomology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.mfo.de/document/0924/OWR_2009_28.pdf"} pdf
          %p Surveys/expositions of this:
          %ul
            %li#Schreiber14a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+generalized+cohomology+in+Cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} Differential generalized cohomology in Cohesive homotopy type theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Semantics of proofs and certified mathematics
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Workshop 1: Formalization of Mathematics
            %li#Schreiber14b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+cohomology+is+Cohesive+homotopy+theory"} Differential cohomology is Cohesive homotopy theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://www.ru.nl/math/research/vmconferences/2014-higher/"} Higher Geometric Structures along the Lower Rhine June 2014
            %li#AmabelDebrayHaine21
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Araminta+Amabel"}> Araminta Amabel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arun+Debray"} Arun Debray
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+J.+Haine"} Peter J. Haine
                (eds.), Section 2.3 in:
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Differential Cohomology: Categories, Characteristic Classes, and Connections
                %a{:href => "https://math.mit.edu/juvitop/pastseminars/2019_Fall.html"} Fall 2019 talks at MIT’s Juvitop seminar
                by: A. Amabel, D. Chua, A. Debray, S. Devalapurkar, D. Freed, P. Haine, M. Hopkins, G. Parker, C. Reid, and A. Zhang. (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.12250"}> arXiv:2109.12250
                )
          %p
            and from the point of view of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+homotopy+type+theory"} modal homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion+and+idelic+structure"} Fractures, Ideles and the Differential Hexagon
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://qcpages.qc.cuny.edu/~swilson/cunyworkshop14.html"} Workshop on differential cohomologies
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://videostreaming.gc.cuny.edu/videos/video/1806/in/channel/55/"} video recording
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+cohesion+and+Arithmetic+geometry"} Differential cohesion and Arithmetic geometry
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.kit.edu/iag3/~herrlich/seite/weihnachts-workshops"} Karslruher Weihnachts-Workshop 2015
          %p#ReferencesFormalizationInCohesiveHoTT
            Formalization in
